# Fork remote & PR policy

This clone works on **PolyFesneauLi/semantica** only.

## Remotes

| Remote | Repo | Allowed |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `origin` | `PolyFesneauLi/semantica` | fetch + **push** + PRs |
| `upstream` | `semantica-agi/semantica` | **fetch only** (pull latest into the fork workflow) |

## Hard rules for the agent

1. **Never push** to `semantica-agi/semantica` (no `git push upstream`, no PR targeting that org unless the user explicitly overrides in writing).
2. **All PRs** mean GitHub PRs **within the fork** (base/head both under `PolyFesneauLi/semantica`), e.g. `lty_branch` → `main` on the fork — not upstream `semantica-agi/semantica`.
3. To refresh from upstream: `git fetch upstream` then merge/rebase `upstream/main` into the current fork branch; push the result only to `origin`.
4. If `upstream` push URL is set to a disable sentinel, do not “fix” it to enable push.
5. Default push target is always `origin` / `origin/<current-branch>` when `LOCAL ≠ main` policy allows.
